  "bandsNote": "drafted 13/10/2026 by scripts/bands.mjs, corrected by hand: the teal topbar (.bg-blue) and the dark header paint their own ground (the draft had root:false and painted a block inside, .features-content, which then covered the features fill's words); the slideshow's owl stage is the photo's frame, not a ground; .ja-topbar (the teal top bar, white words) wears the system's ground and a.button-highlight (the header's Donate now) is a primary button (13/10/2026): both stayed the template's under every system; the GET INVOLVED / OUR VISION cards (.features-content inside the .acm-features.style-1.bg-primary fill) are painted by the template's .bg-primary rule through the surface role: under a system the card fell to the light surface inside the accent band while its title stayed white (white on white under Notion, Airbnb, Stripe; dark on dark under Moxie, visual review 14/10/2026). The card takes the band's ground (paint), its title and words the band's text, and its ghost button (.btn-default: white at 5% with a white line at 20%) inherits the card's words (sideRules, both sides: a fill's paint stops at buttons). The inner pages' green call band (.acm-cta .bg-green, its words set straight in the block) stayed the template's green: it is a fill of the system's (accent first) whose own words take the text that reads on it; 15/10/2026 (v10 inner pages, 4/8 each): the footer painted .item-152 a (the Home item) with the accent on every page, while the template draws only the current item in its colour (.menu-footer .menu > li.active > a, var(--ds-c-accent-text)): on the inner pages the Home link, white on the footer (17.3:1), turned the footer accent, 4.45-4.48:1 under Moxie and Stripe (a mid tone balanced for light and dark words, src/bands.mjs bothSides). The paint now follows the template's own rule, the current item only",
